Green Project (1991): Started at Sun Microsystems.
Developed by James Gosling and his team.
Initially developed for electronic devices and embedded systems.
The language was initially named Oak.
Later, Oak was renamed Java due to trademark issues.
Java was officially announced in 1995.
JDK 1.0 was released on January 23, 1996.
Write Once, Run Anywhere (WORA)
Java is a platform-independent language.
Java code is compiled into bytecode.
Bytecode can run on any operating system with JVM.
The same program can run on Windows, Linux and macOS without modification.
__________
Java 8 (2014): Introduced Lambda Expressions and Stream API.
Java 11 (2018): Introduced HTTP Client and new String methods.
Java 17 (2021): Introduced Sealed Classes.
Java 21 (2023): Introduced Virtual Threads and Sequenced Collections.
Java 25 (2025): Introduced Compact Source Files and Instance Main Methods.
